{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/imagecustomizer","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:12:07.697Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/azurelinux/imagecustomizer/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/azurelinux/imagecustomizer/about"},"readme":"## About\n\nThis repository contains the official Azure Linux Image Customizer container image.\n\n### What is Azure Linux?\n\nAzure Linux is a Linux distribution for Microsoft’s cloud infrastructure and edge products and services. Azure Linux is designed to provide a consistent platform for these devices and services and will enhance Microsoft’s ability to stay current on Linux updates.  \n\nTo learn more about Azure Linux, refer to our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n### What is Azure Linux Image Customizer?\n\nThe Azure Linux Image Customizer is a tool that can take an existing generic Azure Linux image and modify it to be suited for a particular scenario. By providing an Azure Linux base image, users can also supply a config file specifying how they want the image to be customized. For example, this could include the installation of certain RPMs, updating the SELinux mode, and enabling DM-Verity.\n\n## Usage\n\nRefer to the open-source project: [https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/tree/imagecustomizer/stable/toolkit/tools/imagecustomizer](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/tree/imagecustomizer/stable/toolkit/tools/imagecustomizer)\n\n## Support\n\nAzure Linux container images are supported for both internal Microsoft use and public discovery. For more information, please see our [Support Statement](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/-/SUPPORT.md).\n\n## License\n\nThe Azure Linux distribution is provided under the [MIT license](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/-/LICENSE). Individual packages and components are governed by their own licenses i